  <data name="StarttijdenUitleg" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The time slots a plot can get as its start time. Per day type you decide whether a slot can be picked and which block window it stands for; the block number ("Block 3.1") is the slot's place among that day's other slots with a window. So a slot without a window gets no number and does not count — that is how "19:30: Introquest" stays unnumbered.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StarttijdenUitlegBeheer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deleting is not possible: untick all three boxes to take a slot out of the lists without breaking old plots. Renaming is always allowed — the key stays, so the new name appears everywhere. The order follows from the time in the name.</value>
  </data>
